<title>UK: Kvaerner wins China bridge contract.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins China bridge contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A UK subsidiary of Kvaerner, the Norwegian shipbuilding and engineering group, has won a Chinese contract of more than 100 million stg to build one of the world's longest suspension bridges, the Financial Times said.</p>
<p>Kvaerner is due to announce on Monday that Cleveland Structural Engineering has been selected by Jiangsu to build the 1.4 kilometre road bridge over the Yangtze river, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
